Chromium 157.0.8103.30 -> 157.0.8103.33, for the 157.0.8103.30 tarball.

157.0.8103.33 is a tag on the 157 branch (refs/branch-heads/8103) that has
no source tarball (as of 2026-10-30). It has fixes made after
157.0.8103.30: use-after-frees in the bookmarks side panel, MojoCdm,
chrome.windows.update (Extensions) and TransitionPseudoElementData; WebAudio's
media element handler; HttpCache range responses; File System Access's
sensitive paths; re-entry when draining error events; layer changes during a
commit; nested printing; menu items deleted while being inserted;
relatedTarget's cross-origin check; ImageContext access failure
(CVE-2026-118332); V8's maps, prototypes, Maglev and deopt literals; Skia's
SkSL parser, GL BGRA formats, Graphite's paint keys and Ganesh's subset clamp.
Some are likely security fixes that later release notes will credit.

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags (chromium/src
refs/tags/157.0.8103.30..157.0.8103.33), Skia and V8 (the only
dependencies whose DEPS revisions changed; no CIPD/GCS package or gclient
gn arg changed), as served by Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations, CI configuration, PGO pointers, submodule pointer updates,
DEPS.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h and
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h; commit
40aa46194a841a35609fca1cbc7403808b104da0, refs/branch-heads/8103@{#986}).
Dawn's stamps and build/util/MINIBRANCH don't change.

Checked: applies to the 157.0.8103.30 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
157.0.8103.33; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag; the 157.0.8103.30 tarball's non-git files are all classified
(tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

